1. Remote / cloud + Platform work dirs — the real ceiling. Everything reads local
   .nextflow/history + LevelDB cache, and the opt-in layers (--diff-outputs,
   --diff-logs, --diff-dag) all require the tasks' work dirs to still exist on
   this machine. Cloud runs (S3/GCS/Azure work dirs) and Seqera Platform runs
   can't use these layers at all. Reading remote work dirs via Nextflow's own
   filesystem providers, and pulling a run's history/cache from the Platform
   API, would unlock the plugin for the majority of production runs. Highest
   leverage feature on the roadmap.

2. Multi-run / trend view. Everything is strictly pairwise (runA vs runB, or
   --last). A "compare last N as a series" / trend view (e.g. realtime & peak-RSS
   per process across a run series) would turn nf-diff from a two-run comparator
   into a regression-tracking tool — a natural fit given the performance-
   regressions layer already computes signed deltas.
